      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T16:49:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My thoughts on the entire series:\n\nMost of the changes are neatly tucked under-the-hood in core DRM and don\u0027t affect devices until they configure the new `drm.trace\u003d` parameter, which configures additional logging to a new ftrace instance. I personally think these additions as `ANDROID:` are acceptable.\n\nWhile this series is still `ANDROID:` (not yet accepted upstream), it would be best to minimize the impact on drivers and vendor builds by making the changes purely additive.\n\nRather than renaming existing helpers to clarify their focus on \"syslog\" output, I suggest leaving them alone while introducing the new APIs for any driver to opt-in to the new \"drm.trace\" behavior as-needed.",
      "revId": "e67e7d0d2407c51240ef79403e26221a27261e53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
